1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,169
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:07,048
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,184
[gunshots]

7
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:19,269
[T-Bak] <i>Why are there guns?</i>

8
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:20,895
- [gunshots in the distance]
- I can't handle that!

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,147
I'll charge in!

10
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,690
[Karla] I don't want anything
to happen to Brother Atoy.

11
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:24,733
[Paldo] <i>Go inside.</i>

12
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,443
Check how many enemies there are.

13
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,153
- [grunts and groans]
- [gunshots]

14
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:29,070
[grunts]

15
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,447
[Uno] <i>You okay, Emerson?</i>

16
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:31,823
- [Emerson] <i>I'm fine.</i>
- [grunts and groans]

17
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:34,284
[Cita] <i>What? They went there?</i>

18
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:37,203
<i>Are they so angry at the world</i>
<i>that they'd risk their lives?</i>

19
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:39,873
[Denden] <i>Maybe they</i>
<i>just really wanted to help.</i>

20
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,583
[Cita] <i>My God. I hope they'll be safe.</i>

21
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,209
Atoy! [echoing]

22
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:44,294
[gunshot]

23
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,129
- [music swells]
- [gunshot]

24
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:47,297
[clangs]

25
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,214
PREVIOUSLY

26
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,466
[Emerson] <i>Atoy!</i> [echoing]

27
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,050
[gunshots]

28
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,553
[Karla] <i>Hey, foreigner! Look here!</i>

29
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>Put Brother Atoy down!</i>

30
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,139
[Samir speaks in Russian] Shut your mouth!

31
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:57,307
[Karla] <i>Put him down!</i>

32
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,684
[metal clangs]

33
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,187
[gunshots]

34
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,316
[Uno] <i>Good to see you alive, sir.</i>

35
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:07,776
Thank you. Where's Lily?

36
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,153
- [Lily] <i>Where's Samir?</i>
- He escaped.

37
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:12,405
[Atoy] <i>You should call</i>
<i>Colonel Mercado immediately.</i>

38
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:13,448
Are you impressed now?

39
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,784
See? We toppled the enemies.

40
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,368
<i>I don't want anything to happen to you--</i>

41
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:18,870
<i>Of course, I love you.</i>

42
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,789
[teasing]

43
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,832
[T-Bak] <i>You really love us, Brother Atoy!</i>

44
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,252
[Olga] <i>Hold on.</i>
<i>You might not be able to take this.</i>

45
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:29,297
- [Atoy] <i>Why? Did something happen?</i>
- [Olga] <i>You are Ibyang's real father.</i>

46
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,715
She's your child, Atoy.

47
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:33,510
[dramatic sting]

48
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:34,636
[Ibyang] <i>Tatoy?</i>

49
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:47,232
[Ibyang] <i>You're my family?</i>

50
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,067
[Atoy] <i>Yes, Ibyang.</i>

51
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:53,029
[Ibyang sobs] <i>You're… You're my father?</i>

52
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,366
[Atoy] <i>I am.</i>

53
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:01,246
[music swells]

54
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,498
[suave theme music playing]

55
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:05,416
[motorcycle revving]

56
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,335
[sewing machine whirring]

57
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:08,294
[scratches]

58
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,337
[snipping]

59
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:13,216
[sewing machine clacking]

60
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,467
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

61
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:15,426
[thumps and gunshots]

62
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:18,888
- [music intensifies]
- [clicking]

63
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,974
[snipping]

64
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:25,895
- [music swells]
- [electronic blipping]

65
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,940
[music fades]

66
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,821
It's official now?

67
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,198
[softly] Yes.

68
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,992
You're really my Tatoy?

69
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:41,202
[Atoy chuckles softly]

70
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,871
It's very official.

71
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:47,041
[sobs]

72
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:51,045
But… Why?

73
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,508
I spent a long time wondering

74
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:59,095
where my parents were.

75
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:03,224
But they were right beside me all along.

76
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,394
[sobbing]

77
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:09,647
Why didn't we know sooner?

78
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:12,650
Well, Ibyang,

79
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,069
maybe that's just how life is.

80
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:16,613
[sentimental music playing]

81
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:19,991
Sometimes there are things
we just can't explain.

82
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,870
Like threads,

83
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:26,581
tangled together.

84
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,959
But eventually, they straighten out.

85
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:31,753
All of that…

86
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:36,174
is because of Him.

87
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:47,936
But if Mama Olga isn't my mother…

88
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,064
then who is?

89
00:03:54,025 --> 00:03:56,486
[music fades]

90
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,906
[melodramatic music playing]

91
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,243
I know the truth now, Audrey.

92
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:09,374
Janine is not really our child.

93
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:21,886
She is our daughter.

94
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,096
[gasps]

95
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:30,561
- [sobbing]
- [soft drama music playing]

96
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:41,114
[broken voice, in English]
It was you all along.

97
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,494
You are my baby girl.

98
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:49,789
[Audrey, in English] My baby girl.

99
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,583
[sobs, in English] My baby.

100
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:55,837
[sobbing]

101
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:04,012
[Audrey sobbing, in English] I'm so sorry.

102
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,930
Aunt Audrey…

103
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,058
My mama.

104
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,895
My baby.

105
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,939
[sobs] My baby.

106
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:18,026
[sobs]

107
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:24,657
[dramatic music playing]

108
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:29,579
[sobbing]

109
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:45,094
Atoy, thank you for coming back.

110
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:50,683
I'm so happy because
you returned to your family.

111
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:53,311
Thank you, Father.

112
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,856
I prayed for nothing else but…

113
00:05:57,482 --> 00:06:00,943
to have my family whole and…

114
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:03,237
for all of you to be safe.

115
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:07,408
It was granted to you
because you are a good son…

116
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:12,038
and a good man, Atoy.

117
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:17,126
[somber music playing]

118
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,797
Long live Atoy! The son of the thread!

119
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,881
Long live!

120
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:24,300
[all] Long live! Long live!

121
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:28,096
- [cheering]
- [hopeful music playing]

122
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:31,015
[Emerson] Long live Atoy!
The Master Cutter of Tabang Lupa!

123
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:33,935
[cheering, clapping]

124
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:36,229
- [Paldo] Our idol in everything!
- [soft sobbing]

125
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:39,357
[cheering, clapping]

126
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,360
One big community hug!

127
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:45,279
[cheering]

128
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:48,324
[Audrey chuckles]

129
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:51,119
[Audrey sobbing]

130
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:55,081
- [all] Atoy! Atoy!
- Wait.

131
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,084
[all] Atoy! Atoy! Atoy! Atoy!

132
00:06:58,167 --> 00:07:00,628
- Atoy! Atoy! Atoy!
- Ibyang! Ibyang!

133
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:01,921
- Janine.
- [all] Atoy! Atoy!

134
00:07:02,004 --> 00:07:03,297
- Ibyang.
- Janine.

135
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,298
[all] Atoy!

136
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:06,134
[music fades]

137
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:11,681
[melancholic music playing]

138
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:13,766
[smooches]

139
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,435
[speaking softly] Stay here for now.

140
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:25,778
[indistinct]

141
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:34,078
[music fades]

142
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:36,330
Janine, child.

143
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,796
[sobs] I'm sorry.

144
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:48,968
Sorry for… everything I've done.

145
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:50,720
[in English] No, no.

146
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:52,096
You don't need to apologize.

147
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:55,641
[Janine] No.

148
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:59,604
I should ask forgiveness because…

149
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:03,566
I was stubborn.

150
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:06,152
Well,

151
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:11,073
the only reason I did that
is because even if I get scolded,

152
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:14,994
it'll be my mommy and daddy
who will get mad at me, anyway.

153
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,498
I was also demanding,

154
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,666
especially with Daddy.

155
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:27,131
Because this was the first time
I felt what it was like to have a family.

156
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:33,221
And it turns out
you're not really my parents.

157
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:37,058
[gentle music playing]

158
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:38,893
We understand that, Janine.

159
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:44,065
And despite everything that happened…

160
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:51,197
you've become dear to us too, Janine.

161
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,036
I felt that.

162
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,581
So, thank you still,

163
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:04,669
because even for a short while,

164
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:11,133
I felt what it was like to have
a family and be part of one.

165
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:13,678
[sobs]

166
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:15,221
Can I

167
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:19,559
not go back to Mama Roma?

168
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:23,604
Can you just take me to the orphanage?

169
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:29,569
Why?

170
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:33,281
Who said you were going back there?

171
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:36,951
[Atoy] You have a home.

172
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,872
We will adopt you, Janine. [sniffles]

173
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,710
[sobbing]

174
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:47,169
Child…

175
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,380
[sobbing]

176
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:51,591
We love you very much.

177
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:54,343
[sobbing]

178
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:57,179
But Ibyang…

179
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:02,685
I even told her to leave.

180
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:05,896
She'll just be angry with me.

181
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:07,857
Ibyang?

182
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:13,237
She's tough, but she's kind.

183
00:10:14,739 --> 00:10:18,534
Do you know, when she learned the truth,

184
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:21,871
she was sad and worried for you, child.

185
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,000
She even looked for you.

186
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:31,714
So, I'm sure
she'll understand our decision.

187
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:33,549
[in English] Okay?

188
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:40,056
[in English] Thank you. Thank you.

189
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,976
Come, my child. Let's go.

190
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,896
[sobbing]

191
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:04,080
[music fades]

192
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:05,206
[reporter, in English]
<i>It has been identified</i>

193
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:08,459
<i>that the exchange of gunfire</i>
<i>that happened earlier today</i>

194
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:12,838
<i>was caused by the secret army connected</i>
<i>to the current ambassador of Zahran,</i>

195
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,548
<i>Viktor Petrov.</i>

196
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:17,676
[in English] <i>As of the moment,</i>
<i>they are trying to reach Mr. Petrov,</i>

197
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,595
<i>but he is nowhere to be found.</i>

198
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:24,100
[suspicious music playing]

199
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:29,563
Hon, look. Isn't that Atoy? There, see.

200
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,235
[in English] Yes. It's him.

201
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:35,528
So, what now?

202
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:38,030
That means he might already
be with Audrey.

203
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:39,698
[in English] Good.

204
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:41,659
[Martina, in English] Good?

205
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:42,952
This is a problem.

206
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,078
[in English] It's not.

207
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,664
Because if we see Atoy,

208
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:50,251
then most likely he and Audrey
are together in one place.

209
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:53,003
It will be easier to erase them
from the world.

210
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,423
[Red] So, if I were them,
I'd enjoy it while it lasts.

211
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:56,674
[music fades]

212
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:58,592
I'll take them all down at once.

213
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:02,179
[tense music playing]

214
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:03,180
I slammed him against the wall.

215
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,098
- Oh?
- Oh, yes.

216
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:05,015
Then I twisted his arm.

217
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:07,226
- And I brushed his chest with punches!
- That's amazing!

218
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:08,269
He died. It swelled.

219
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,311
- [group] Ah.
- Dead, yes!

220
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:10,438
- Wasn't that--
- Dead, as in dead.

221
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:11,605
Uno did that, right?

222
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:12,648
- Yes.
- Oh!

223
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:13,566
[Emerson] No, just a little--

224
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:15,609
I knew it. Your stories sound exaggerated.

225
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,735
- No, he did little…
- Well, me,

226
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:18,904
- …Uno did little--
- I believe Emerson!

227
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:20,906
- You're my number one hero!
- [teasing]

228
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,702
Wow, wow! So sweet!
Like what I'm drinking! Hmm!

229
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:27,997
- I'll sip your eyes!
- [laughing]

230
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:31,041
But we really need to celebrate!

231
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,585
Not just Atoy's safety,

232
00:12:32,668 --> 00:12:35,087
but Tabang Lupa's safety!

233
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,547
Exactly! That's right!
That's how it should be!

234
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,382
I'm game! I'll help you.

235
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:40,301
- [Siony] Okay. Oh!
- Okay, huh. So--

236
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,845
- Yes.
- So how do we celebrate?

237
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:44,555
- Uh, I know!
- [Nestor] What?

238
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:45,556
[in English] Boodle fight!

239
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:46,682
[exclaiming]

240
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:49,351
[all, in English] Boodle fight!
Boodle fight!

241
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:50,853
- [in English] Yes!
- [all, in English] Boodle fight!

242
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:54,815
Thank you, Lord, for not abandoning us

243
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:58,986
and for keeping us away from harm.

244
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,615
All of us.

245
00:13:02,698 --> 00:13:06,368
[gentle music playing]

246
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:12,124
Lord, and to you also, San Antonio.

247
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,337
Thank you for not abandoning us.

248
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,633
Thank you for everything. First,

249
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:26,514
for friends, true friends
who were really there for us.

250
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:33,062
Second, for giving me
courage and strength.

251
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,107
And third,

252
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,569
for giving us a child.

253
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,655
[gentle music playing]

254
00:13:42,738 --> 00:13:44,281
[soft chuckle]

255
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:49,119
Even before we asked,
she was already here.

256
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:51,247
She had been with us all along.

257
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,167
Thank you, Lord.

258
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:58,170
In the name of the Father, the Son,
and the Holy Spirit…

259
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:08,556
Child, from now on, I promise you,
I will do everything for you.

260
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:13,352
Hmm. Because I'm your child,

261
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:17,064
your love for me is times ten million?

262
00:14:17,147 --> 00:14:21,694
Oh, not just ten million.
Ten billion or even a trillion!

263
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:24,947
Oh, wow.

264
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:30,077
So, I can still be pesky?

265
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,412
[light music playing]

266
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:34,748
Hmm. Pesky? That's what you must never do.

267
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:38,085
Because if you are, I'll still scold you.

268
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:40,421
Hmph.

269
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:44,174
You're not Master Grumpy anymore,
now you're Daddy Grumpy.

270
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:46,552
- [Audrey chuckles softly]
- Just joking!

271
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,807
I still can't believe it.

272
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:56,896
I've been with my parents all along.

273
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,272
I just didn't know.

274
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,443
Us too, my child.

275
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:07,823
I'm just happy
that even though our paths strayed,

276
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,409
we still found each other…

277
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:15,664
and we didn't lose you, child.

278
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:17,791
[chuckles softly]

279
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:19,960
Hmm. [smooches]

280
00:15:22,838 --> 00:15:24,715
[Audrey] Hmm… [sighs]

281
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:26,717
- Tatoy.
- Oh?

282
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,262
Where is Mama Olga?

283
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:35,643
[light music playing]

284
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,436
Here it is. I'll do it.

285
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:38,979
I'll do it, I'll do it. That's it.

286
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:39,897
- Let's go.
- [Karla] Let's go.

287
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,399
[in English] Karla! Do you need help?

288
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,944
Karla, I'll do the talking.

289
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,446
I'll handle it.

290
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,115
No, bro. We're fine.

291
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,451
Just a moment.

292
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:53,827
- Is that okay?
- [Karla] Yes.

293
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:55,663
Okay. [sighs]

294
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:59,416
So, since your mission here is done,

295
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,834
are you leaving?

296
00:16:00,918 --> 00:16:02,419
[sneaky music playing]

297
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:04,213
I don't know yet.

298
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:08,008
But maybe.

299
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:11,595
Yes. Just for a short while.
Just a short while.

300
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,266
Do you like Karla?

301
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:19,478
Why, bro?

302
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:22,106
You, do you like Karla?

303
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,607
Yes.

304
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,484
Then why did you choose someone else?

305
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,987
[chuckles]

306
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:30,739
You know, the people here told me…

307
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,411
you never courted Karla before.

308
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:39,123
You let your chances pass.

309
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:42,626
And now, when you learned someone
else might court her,

310
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:47,131
suddenly you make a move. What's that?

311
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:48,590
What's that, bro?

312
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,093
You know,

313
00:16:52,177 --> 00:16:54,805
that's not a good move.

314
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:58,308
Because you like her,

315
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,185
but you're too late, bro.

316
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:01,437
- [chuckles softly]
- [sighs]

317
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:02,813
There's nothing wrong with that.

318
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:05,399
People's feelings can change.

319
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:09,194
[in English] Gavin. Babe!

320
00:17:09,903 --> 00:17:11,238
[in English] Where have you been?
I've been looking for you.

321
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,700
[chuckles softly] You're making a move,
but you already have a girlfriend.

322
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:15,784
[chuckles softly] Let's go.

323
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,828
[Uno] Maybe they're looking for him there.

324
00:17:18,412 --> 00:17:19,580
- [Denden mutters]
- Excuse me!

325
00:17:19,663 --> 00:17:21,081
[Karla, indistinct]

326
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,499
- [in English] Babe.
- [sniffles]

327
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:24,585
[in English] Hello? [chuckles softly]

328
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:26,378
What happened to you?

329
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:29,715
I've been trying to call you,
but you didn't answer.

330
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:33,302
- Are you ghosting me?
- I have personal problems.

331
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:36,430
[in English] Aww. That's too bad.

332
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:40,184
[in English] Um, anyway…

333
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:44,063
I was invited by couple influencers.

334
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:47,649
They want to collab,
and since it's for couples,

335
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,486
I need you to join me! It's for charity.

336
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:54,364
[in English] For charity or for yourself?

337
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:55,532
[in English] What?

338
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:59,411
You just want to do this
for your followers.

339
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,705
To pretend in front of them.

340
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,415
But in truth, you don't want to do this.

341
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:06,085
Just now, I told you
I have personal problems.

342
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:08,212
[in English] But you didn't bother
to ask me about it.

343
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:10,214
Don't you care about me?

344
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:15,385
The people here in Tabang Lupa
are more genuine.

345
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:17,346
More genuine?

346
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,890
Who's more genuine?

347
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:21,809
Your friend? Karla?

348
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:22,976
[in English] Yes.

349
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:29,691
[pensive music playing]

350
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:31,193
Ibyang,

351
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:36,490
the reason I wanted to help
save your Daddy Atoy is because…

352
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,994
I want you to be happy.

353
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:45,040
[gentle music playing]

354
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,875
I'm sorry for…

355
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,504
lying to you.

356
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:54,424
Sorry also for being strict with you.

357
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:57,678
Forgive me.

358
00:18:58,262 --> 00:18:59,596
It's okay.

359
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,224
I'm not angry.

360
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:06,937
My love for you won't change, Mama Olga.

361
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:09,773
Really?

362
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:14,236
Yes. I'm thankful.

363
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:17,322
[Ibyang] Because I met you.

364
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:21,285
Because even if you're my fake mama,

365
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:27,583
you're the reason
I'm now with my real parents.

366
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:32,379
Thank you so much, Mama Olga.

367
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:41,680
You know, you'll be
a best actress someday.

368
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:44,850
- You cry so well!
- Hey!

369
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,686
This isn't TV-series acting.

370
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:49,271
These are real tears.

371
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:54,193
But seriously, Ibyang.

372
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,738
I'll really miss you.

373
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:02,326
You know, if Atoy weren't your father,

374
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,995
and you hadn't found your real parents,

375
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,664
I would adopt you.

376
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:10,542
Thank you very much.

377
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,962
I'll miss you too, Mama Olga.

378
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,926
- [soft drama music playing]
- [sobs]

379
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,302
[Atoy] Olga, thank you.

380
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:23,680
You completed my family.

381
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:29,603
If you miss Ibyang, just call.

382
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,271
Is video call okay?

383
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:37,319
Because when I get to the States,
I might be busy.

384
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,239
I'm claiming it…

385
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:44,368
I'll be famous
when my Hollywood film comes out.

386
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,911
Ah, Hollywood?

387
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,788
Wow! Really?

388
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:49,498
- Yes!
- That's amazing.

389
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:50,749
Right?

390
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:53,210
[chuckles softly]

391
00:20:53,293 --> 00:20:55,003
Okay then. [sniffles]

392
00:20:55,879 --> 00:20:56,880
Uh…

393
00:20:59,299 --> 00:21:02,970
[music fades]

394
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:07,432
[melodramatic music playing]

395
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,484
[smooches]

396
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:18,443
[sobs] Goodbye.

397
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:21,905
- [Atoy] Take care.
- Take care.

398
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:24,658
- [Olga] I'll go ahead.
- [softly] Okay.

399
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:33,583
[Cita] Sorry, I just accompanied
Janine upstairs.

400
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,085
I'll go ahead.

401
00:21:38,922 --> 00:21:40,841
Uh, Godmother.

402
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:53,312
I'm sorry if I kept you out of my life.

403
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,232
Because, well, that's how it is.

404
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:00,485
Even after all these years…

405
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:04,239
it still hurts.

406
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:11,038
I understand you, Atoy.

407
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:14,416
I was the one at fault.

408
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,460
I made the mistake.

409
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,379
I get why you're angry.

410
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,382
That's just it.

411
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:28,096
[sighs] I couldn't bring myself
to be angry at you, because…

412
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:33,727
of course, I already consider you
as my mother.

413
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:37,355
[sighs] So even if it hurts…

414
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:43,487
the good things you did for me
outweigh it.

415
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:46,656
[soft drama music playing]

416
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:49,451
Atoy…

417
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:50,619
Godmother.

418
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:56,041
Let's just forget everything
that happened.

419
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:04,091
No… No.

420
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:06,426
No, Atoy.

421
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,677
[sobs]

422
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:10,305
- No.
- Godmother, let's just forget it.

423
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:15,644
I need to tell you this. [sobs]

424
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:21,149
I need to face it
and accept all my mistakes.

425
00:23:22,275 --> 00:23:23,527
[sobs]

426
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:25,487
I confessed to Julie.

427
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:30,325
My conscience was eating me alive.

428
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:34,871
[sobbing] And I'm thankful she forgave me.

429
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:39,000
She even entrusted you
and your father to me, Atoy.

430
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:41,837
[sobs]

431
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:47,801
I don't expect you to forgive me
the way your mother did,

432
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:49,136
but…

433
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:50,137
but--

434
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,555
- [sobs]
- Godmother…

435
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:55,392
[sobbing]

436
00:23:58,228 --> 00:23:59,312
It's okay.

437
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,273
[sobbing]

438
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:03,108
We're family.

439
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:09,656
- I forgive you.
- [sobbing]

440
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,201
[music fades]

441
00:24:13,285 --> 00:24:15,495
I don't want to lose a mother again.

442
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:17,622
Mmm.

443
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:20,625
[sobbing]

444
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:25,755
I'm right here, son.

445
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:28,800
My child?

446
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:31,553
[both chuckle]

447
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,430
- [sobbing]
- [softly] Thank you.

448
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:34,973
[Cita] Thank you.

449
00:24:35,056 --> 00:24:36,600
[sobbing]

450
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:41,521
[melodramatic music playing]

451
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:48,820
[sobs]

452
00:24:49,529 --> 00:24:51,573
Godmother, you know…

453
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:52,741
[chuckles softly]

454
00:24:53,408 --> 00:24:54,910
It's crazy.

455
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:58,580
Being locked up that long
makes you so hungry.

456
00:24:58,663 --> 00:24:59,497
[chuckles]

457
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:01,875
So, can I ask a favor?

458
00:25:01,958 --> 00:25:05,462
Can you cook my favorite tinola,
Godmother?

459
00:25:05,545 --> 00:25:09,549
Tinola with lots of green papaya
and chili leaves?

460
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:11,301
- That's it!
- Of course!

461
00:25:11,384 --> 00:25:13,011
You'll be spoiled!

462
00:25:13,094 --> 00:25:14,638
But I'll cook it tomorrow, okay?

463
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:18,225
Tomorrow? Why tomorrow, Godmother?

464
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:20,393
- Because they prepared a feast--
- I'm so hungry--

465
00:25:20,477 --> 00:25:23,480
Because Father Peping and Kapitana
prepared a feast for you,

466
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:25,315
to celebrate your return.

467
00:25:25,982 --> 00:25:29,319
Oh? Why? I'm not an overseas worker.

468
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:30,946
[chuckles]

469
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:34,658
Everyone's just happy
because you're home, Atoy.

470
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:39,371
[music fades]

471
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:43,124
[phone ringing]

472
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:46,044
[tense music playing]

473
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:47,337
[in English] Hello, sir?

474
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:50,882
[music swells]

475
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:53,009
[electronic blipping]

476
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:56,096
[intense music playing]

477
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:03,520
- [groans]
- You're the bald devil!

478
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:05,563
- [Nestor] Hey!
- Get your filthy hands off Ibyang!

479
00:26:05,647 --> 00:26:07,065
- No! Let me go!
- [Kurt grunts]

480
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,108
- Brother Kurt!
- Let's go!

481
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:09,192
[in English] Hello, Red!

482
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:10,735
Ah, you monster! You demon!

483
00:26:11,444 --> 00:26:13,363
Where are the children?
Give me back the children!

484
00:26:13,446 --> 00:26:16,992
I'll make these kids suffer.
I'll profit from them.

485
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:20,662
That's one of the major concentration
camps of the terrorist group Obsidian.

486
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:22,914
That's the international
human trafficking syndicate.

487
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:24,833
If that's where they were taken,
what do we do?

488
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:26,084
How do we get them back?

489
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:28,086
No matter what happens,
I'll get our child.

490
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:29,087
UP NEXT

491
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:31,381
If this has to be my last mission,
I'll do it.

492
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:33,800
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

493
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:37,095
♪ <i>One cut, and it's done</i> ♪

494
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,346
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

495
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:40,473
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
